# Build-context hygiene. Added on the dual-B60 experiment branch, but it protects
# EVERY image built from this repo, including tier 1 and tier 2.
#
# Why this exists: docker/Dockerfile.arcint does `COPY . /src/arcint`. Without an
# ignore file, ANY secret that wanders into the build context is copied into a
# published image layer — where it stays recoverable forever, even if a later
# RUN step deletes it. There is no way to remove a layer's contents after the fact.
#
# This file is the cheapest possible insurance against that. Keep it strict.

# --- git --------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- secrets and credential material ---------------------------------------
# These must NEVER reach an image layer under any circumstances.
.env
.env.*
*.env
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
*_rsa
*_ed25519
*credentials*
*secret*
*.token
.netrc
_netrc
.aws/
.ssh/
.kube/
.npmrc
.docker/

# --- operator-local / agent-local files ------------------------------------
# Fork- and machine-specific narrative; never upstream-facing, never in an image.
CLAUDE.local.md
*.local.md
*.local.md.tmp.*
*.local.md.bak*
review.md
.scratch/
.claude/
.pi/

# --- build output ----------------------------------------------------------
build/
build*/
cmake-build*/
out/
dist/
*.o
*.a
*.so
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.cache/
node_modules/

# --- logs and scratch ------------------------------------------------------
*.log
tools/flash-next-watch.log
*.tmp
*.bak
tmp/

# --- model weights ---------------------------------------------------------
# Model artifacts are NEVER baked into an image layer: they are tens of GB, make
# every pull slow, hit registry size limits, and force a re-pull on every rebuild.
# They are bind-mounted at runtime. If a weights directory ever appears in the
# tree, ignore it here rather than letting a COPY pick it up.
/models/**
!/models/allowlist-raw.json

# --- images and archives ---------------------------------------------------
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.iso

# --- docs that are not needed at build time --------------------------------
# Kept deliberately small: the build reads DESIGN.md/CHANGELOG.md paths in a few
# tests, so we do not exclude docs wholesale.
